{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner finding, live, 11:36 Eastern: the smart-HTTP read client of packages/git (http-read.ts, the pack trailer check) refuses every read of a repository on the hosting own Git service with hash-mismatch: pack trailer, because that service answers git-upload-pack with 0008NAK, the raw pack, and then a flush packet 0000 after the pack; the client takes everything after NAK as the pack, so the trailer it compares ends in 0000. The pack verifies once the trailing flush packet is left out, and git index-pack accepts it. Captured responses are committed as fixtures on planner/site-fixture at 5c981c6d (packages/git/test/fixtures/own-host, no token in them). This explains the site route 502 (x-site-step objects) and would affect any destination read over smart HTTP on that host (the own-host provider ref and objects reads; the founding push itself succeeded because the push client is separate). The fix is handed to the site cloud session: parse the pack by its structure and ignore bytes after the trailer, with a test on the captured bytes and a control. Builder: the GitHub path is not affected.","body":{"finding":"upload-pack-flush","fixtures":"planner/site-fixture@5c981c6d"}}